"},{"type":"units","items":[{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 175","status":"inactive"}],"units":4,"label":"Small Jazz Combo","notes":"Complete 4 units from:"},{"type":"units","items":[{"type":"text","text":"Global Jazz Studies 176A through 176G"}],"units":8,"label":"Large Jazz Ensemble","notes":"Complete 8 units of large jazz ensemble from Global Jazz Studies 176A through 176G:"}],"label":"Performance (24 units)","notes":"Students must enroll in a studio class and at least one combo or ensemble each quarter."},{"type":"units","items":[{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 122A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 122B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 122C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 127A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 127B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 127C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 129A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 129B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 129C","status":"inactive"}],"units":24,"label":"Musicianship and Theory (24 units)","notes":"Complete 24 units from:"},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 101","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 125","status":"inactive"},{"type":"choose","items":[{"type":"course","code":"AF AMER 108","status":"active"},{"type":"course","code":"AF AMER M150D","status":"active"},{"type":"course","code":"AF AMER M158C","status":"active"}],"count":1,"label":"African American Studies","notes":"Select one course (at least 4 units) from:"},{"type":"choose","items":[{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS M109","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS M119","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS M130","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS M131","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 165","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 188","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 199","status":"inactive"}],"count":1,"label":"Global Jazz Studies","notes":"Select one course (at least 4 units) from:"},{"type":"choose","items":[{"type":"course","code":"MSC IND 2","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"MSC IND 104A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"MSC IND 107A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"MSC IND 115A","status":"inactive"}],"count":1,"label":"Music Industry","notes":"Select one course (at least 4 units) from:"}],"label":"Scholarly Foundations (20 units)","notes":"Complete Global Jazz Studies 101, 125 and one course (at least 4 units) from each subject area listed, for a total of 20 units."},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 186A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"GJ STDS 186B","status":"inactive"}],"label":"Capstone Seminar and Project (4 units)"}],"label":"The Major"}}],"narrative":[],"overrides_applied":[]},"nodes":[{"id":"AF AMER 108","title":"Jazz and Political Imagination","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["The Major: African American Studies"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. How has jazz come to symbolize so many different political tendencies—freedom and democratic values, threat to order and civil society, possibility of integration and racial harmony, Black liberation and nationalism, conservatism, surrealism, socialism, etc., throughout 20th century? What about jazz enables people to read their political aspirations and hopes in what is primarily instrumental, improvised music? Exploration of history of ideas about jazz, specifically how writers, activists, movements, and musicians understood politics of jazz. Exploration of political imaginations—here and abroad—in particular in jazz and question of freedom—social freedom, political freedom, cultural, and artistic freedom. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/AFAMER108"},{"id":"AF AMER M150D","title":"Recent African American Urban History: Funk Music and Politics of Black Popular Culture","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["The Major: African American Studies"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Same as History M150D.) Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour (when scheduled). Designed for juniors/seniors. Exploration of musical genre known as funk that emerged in its popular form during late 1960s and reached popular high point, in black culture, during 1970s. Funk, fusion of gospel, blues, jazz, rhythm and blues, soul, rock, and many other musical styles, offers students unique window into recent African American history. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/AFAMERM150D"},{"id":"AF AMER M158C","title":"Introduction to Afro-American History","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"upper","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["The Major: African American Studies"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"(Same as History M150C.) Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour (when scheduled). Designed for juniors/seniors. Survey of Afro-American experience, with emphasis on three great transitions of Afro-American life: transition from Africa to New World slavery, transition from slavery to freedom, and transition from rural to urban milieus. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/AFAMERM158C"},{"id":"ETHNMUS 20B","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"level":"","status":"inactive","in_major":true,"role":"choice","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Musical Cultures of the World"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":""},{"id":"ETHNMUS 20C","title":"","units":"","offered":[],"